Branch: nkela/sa8255p_v6_11_rc2
Description:
	This branch is created to enable support for SA8255p Qualcomm SoC and
Ride platform used in Automotive BU. This platform uses SCMI power, reset,
performance,sensor protocols for resources(e.g. clocks, regulator, phy etc.)
voting. SA8255p is a virtual platforms that uses Qualcomm smc/hvc transport
driver.
	Multiple SCMI virtual instances are being used to achieve the
parallelism. SCMI plaform running in SMP enabled VM allows us to send/service multiple
resource requests in parallel. Each device is assigned its dedicated SCMI
channel and Tx/Rx doorbells.
	Resources operations are grouped together to achieve better
abstraction and reduce the # of requests being sent to SCMI platform(server)
hence improving boot time KPIs. This design approach was present in LinaroConnect
2024[1].

